Write a Verilog module named `iir8_v7`, an order-8 IIR filter with inputs `clk`, active-low `rst_n`, an 8-bit unsigned sample input `x`, and a 16-bit registered output `y`. Each cycle compute y[n] = (sum over k=0..8 of B[k]*x[n-k]) + ((9*y[n-1])>>4) + ((5*y[n-2])>>4), keeping only the low 16 bits (mod 2^16), where the feedforward coefficients are B = [57, 40, 15, 4, 33, 61, 39, 57, 30] (B[0] applies to the current sample) and y[n-1], y[n-2] are the previous two outputs. Clear all state to 0 on `!rst_n`.

Use exactly this module interface (port names and widths must match):

module iir8_v7 (
  input clk, input rst_n, input [7:0] x, output reg [15:0] y
);

Write standard synthesizable Verilog-2001. Active-low rst_n clears the outputs; outputs are registered on posedge clk.

